{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"15515","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/15515","key":"MC-214662","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"09/Feb/21 10:13 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p><b>The resource pack attached to \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-214686\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-214686\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Wall torch template model is called &quot;template_torch_wall.json&quot;\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-214686\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n offers a complete fix for this issue. Mojang have my full permission to (and are encouraged to) replace the affected vanilla model files with the contents of the resource pack.</b></p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Thebug\"></a>The bug</h3>\n<p>The torches on redstone repeaters and redstone comparators appear darker than expected, and are shaded depending on the view direction. This is not the case with redstone torches themselves, which are fully lit regardless of the view direction.</p>\n\n<p>This began in 1.8, and was not the case in 1.7 or earlier. In addition, this is not the case in Bedrock Edition, effectively also making this a parity issue.</p>\n\n<p>While this was listed in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-68302\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-68302\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Some 2D blocks models are shaded incorrectly\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-68302\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n, I still strongly consider this behaviour unintended for many reasons, including the two stated above. In addition, MC-67830's resolution contradicts such an assertion of this being intended. Other reasons are listed in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro\" data-jira-key=\"MC-236474\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-236474\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Melon and pumpkin stems appear much darker than they should\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-236474\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-complete jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Reopened</span>\n            </span>\n, a very similar issue.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce\"></a>How to reproduce</h3>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Place down a redstone torch, noting how bright it appears when in the \"on\" state</li>\n\t<li>Place down a redstone repeater in a way that the torch powers it</li>\n\t<li>Note that the torches on said redstone repeater are darker than the standalone torch</li>\n\t<li>Now place down a comparator which also receives power</li>\n\t<li>Note that it, too, has darker torches than one would expect</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"Expectedbehaviour\"></a>Expected behaviour</h3>\n<p>The torches on repeaters and comparators would appear as bright as redstone torches themselves</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Actualbehaviour\"></a>Actual behaviour</h3>\n<p>Repeater and comparator torches are noticeably darker</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtofix\"></a>How to fix</h3>\n<p>The resource pack attached to \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-214686\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-214686\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Wall torch template model is called &quot;template_torch_wall.json&quot;\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-214686\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n fixes this issue completely.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"10/Feb/21 8:51 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/25180","id":"25180","filename":"2021-02-09_17.43.30.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"muzikbike","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Dublin","accountType":"customer"},"created":"09/Feb/21 10:12 AM","size":"297 kB","mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/25180","thumbnail":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/thumbnail/25180"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/25181","id":"25181","filen